        Heading("Where to start", id: "where-to-start").h2

        Markdown("- **To learn WebFluent:** read [Getting started](/docs/guide/getting-started), work through the [tutorial](/docs/guide/tutorial), then read the *Concepts* section in order. Every example in them builds. For more practice, try the [three project tutorials](/docs/tutorials/todos).\n- **To understand it coming from a framework:** read [Coming from React, Vue or Svelte](/docs/guide/coming-from) first. It maps what you know to what is here.\n- **To build a feature:** go to the *Guides* page that names the task.\n- **To look something up:** use the reference chapters, starting with the [components reference](/reference). They are generated from the compiler, or checked against it.\n- **To fix a problem:** start at [Troubleshooting](/docs/guide/troubleshooting). Every diagnostic code has an entry in [Diagnostics](/errors).\n\nThe test suite parses, type-checks and compiles every `wf` code block in this guide, so what you read is what the compiler accepts. A block that leaves something out says so with a `…`.")

        Heading("Versions", id: "versions").h2

        Markdown("This guide describes WebFluent 6, the stable line. Run `wf --version` to see which release you have. [Upgrading](/docs/guide/upgrading) lists what changed in each release.")
    }
}
